# PHP (services/cecf-wordpress) — never trust a host-local composer
# install; every Docker build must produce its own vendor/ from
# composer.lock so it matches what a clean Render checkout builds.
**/vendor
services/cecf-wordpress/web/wp
services/cecf-wordpress/web/app/plugins/*
!services/cecf-wordpress/web/app/plugins/.gitkeep
services/cecf-wordpress/web/app/uploads/*
!services/cecf-wordpress/web/app/uploads/.gitkeep

# Never trust a host-local `vite dev` run either — public/hot is the file
# Vite's @vite() Blade directive checks to decide "dev server is running,
# emit http://[::1]:5173/... asset URLs"; if it leaks in from the host
# (mirroring web/app/plugins above) the built image silently points every
# CSS/JS tag at a dev server that doesn't exist in the container, and
# nothing loads. public/build (the real production assets) still comes
# from the theme-build stage's COPY --from=, not from here.
services/cecf-wordpress/web/app/themes/cecf-sage/public/*
!services/cecf-wordpress/web/app/themes/cecf-sage/public/.gitkeep
